1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Sathi: synthetic local prototype. This walkthrough is assembled from actual UI captures, not continuous real-time screen recording. All fees and limits are ASSUMPTIONS.

2
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The scoped agent requests 3,000 BDT. The customer sees payout 3,000, assumed fee 45, and ledger debit 3,045, then confirms using Bangla digits. The customer receives no terminal code.

3
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Only the bound terminal issues the one-time expiring code after verification. Actual redemption succeeded. Duplicate issuance and replay were rejected. Active codes are omitted from this recording.

4
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:30,000
The Bangla receipt comes from the durable database ledger. It states the payable amount and does not prove physical cash delivery. A 2,800 BDT customer report creates a 200 BDT gap case; assumed tolerance is 60 BDT.

5
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:50,000
A separate 3,000 BDT request with customer confirmation 2,500 stays requested after the first mismatch and is rejected after the second. Cases 6 and 7 are saved for human review.

6
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The analyst reviews actual PostgreSQL cases. Escalating cash-gap case 5 is recorded in the audit. Human review and model scores never grant redemption. Startup preserves spent balances and cases.

7
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Outreach displays saved synthetic predictions with frozen provenance and SHAP reasons in raw log-odds. Agent risks use observed signals and train-derived volume peers; scores are review priorities, not proven fraud.

8
00:02:30,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Held-out assisted PR-AUC: model 0.8091, rule 0.6967. Agent ensemble: 2/2 skimmers, 0/4 honest high-volume false flags; precision at 15 is 2/15. Shifted Isolation Forest falsely flags 3/4; subtle skimmers are missed. Idealized adoption is not measured field benefit.
